Retain the reviewed ACPI/OF applicability, duplicate-prompt removal,
firmware-node lifetime, return-value, fixed-clock build, CRTC reporting and
eDP lifecycle corrections from the CIX display queue. Exclude the fixed-MMIO
reset, mutable engineering controls and incomplete HDCP test interfaces which
are handled by the following production-hardening patch.

Demote probe routing, graph topology and CRTC assignment details to DRM or
device debug output while retaining hardware discovery and actionable failures
at their existing severities. When the PWM backlight is modular, request it
before the CIX DisplayPort module so the eDP supplier is available without
turning the optional backlight into a hard link dependency.

This artifact is mechanically regenerated from the exact Linux 7.1.5 CIX
preimage immediately after patch 70120.

